# Copy to .env and edit before running `make up`.
#
# The control plane never connects to a target Kubernetes cluster directly — no
# kubeconfig, no cluster credentials, no cluster-facing env vars belong here at
# all. Each cluster's own cluster-agent (installed via `make cluster-agent-up
# CLUSTER=<name>`) is the only thing with real k8s credentials; it polls this
# control plane for work and pushes status/metrics back. See
# controlplane/settings/clusters.yaml for how target clusters are registered,
# and controlplane/shared/queuebackend for how admission never dials out.
#
# There is currently nothing this file needs to set — it exists so `make
# controlplane-up`'s `cp .env.example .env` step has something to copy.
